WEBVTT

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.450
Hey, how many pages will the quiz cover?

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.780
Um, he told us yesterday.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.250
But seriously...

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.340
Morning!

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.470
Wait, you cut your hair?

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:49.390
Looks cute.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.430
Yo, morning.

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:56.950
Oh, morning...

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.040
Hey, you free after school?

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:00.710
Uh-huh.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.840
Mind stopping somewhere on the way home?

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.060
Eh? Where?

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.390
The usual place.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.380
The usual place?

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.840
Count me in.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.240
Appreciate it...

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:11.110
Sure.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:11.860
Thanks.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:12.980
Yep.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.760
Kasuga!

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:37.670
<b>Flowers of Evil</b>

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:37.670
<b>Episode 1 of 13</b>

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.510
And then,

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.320
he suddenly got really pissed!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.680
I didn't get pissed.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.590
Right, Kojima?

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.180
Beats me.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.810
Kasuga, you don't play many games, do you?

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.870
I do sometimes,

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.630
but they aren't really my thing.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.900
Stop playing it cool!

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.390
Cut it out!

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.030
Okay, take your seats.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.030
Come on, Yamada!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:48.090
I'm a junior high school student in Ba...

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.720
Ba... B-Bangkok.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.420
More practice, Mr. Kojima.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.960
Next, Ms. Saeki.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:00.350
Yes.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.860
We have our New Year's Festival

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:10.780
on April 13th, 14th, and 15th.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.790
We call it Songkran.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.870
During this festival, people...

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.170
Here goes.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.770
Thighs without any meat on them 
don't count as thighs.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.980
What, you want thunder thighs?

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.410
Nice, Nanako.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.730
That was awesome, Nanako!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.420
<b>Girls Changing! 
No Boys Allowed!!</b>

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.420
Can I use your hairbrush?

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.420
Sure.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:02.700
I put on weight again.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.180
What? You're so skinny.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.480
Where are you looking?

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:06.840
I don't see anything.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:07.420
Look at my tummy.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.870
Did you buy volume 8, Kojima?

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.390
As soon as it hit the shelf.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.470
Wasn't it great?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.380
Totally.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.060
It ruled.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.970
Let me borrow it sometime...

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.290
You always get food all over my stuff.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.470
Oh, that's bad.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.030
Don't make up crap.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.760
Potato chips are the worst.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.600
Rice crackers, too.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.540
Oh, really?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.380
And then, Shimoyama showed up in his sweats.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.900
Yeah, I wonder where he got that thing.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.410
That color is freaky.

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:48.670
Oh, crap!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.390
H-Hey...

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.510
Wait!

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.020
<b>Japanese Quiz</b>

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:27.760
<i>"A sky-throned sphinx, unknown yet, I combine</i>

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:32.730
<i>The cygnet's whiteness with a heart of snow.</i>

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:38.070
<i>I loathe all movement that displaces line,</i>

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:43.030
<i>And neither tears nor laughter do I know."</i>

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.020
Okay!

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.710
Time's up!

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.030
Come on, pick romance...

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.070
Nah, I vote for horror.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.240
Horror? Really?

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.270
Dude, I can't do horror.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.140
It's too much.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.380
Same here.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:05.900
Yeah.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:08.900
But fear and laughter are 
similar in their essences.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:09.900
Huh?

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:10.820
What?

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:12.140
No way!

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:14.810
Both fear and laughter require 
an element of surprise.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:17.160
Yeah, yeah. You probably 
read that in a book.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.260
It's true...

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.380
It's common sense.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:21.430
Makes sense.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.720
There are some funny horror movies.

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.540
Like <i>Army of Darkness</i>.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.640
See?

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.020
Hey, let's drop by Kojima's place today.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:33.840
He has volume 8.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.590
Yeah, we can grab ice cream.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.600
You mean that cola-flavored stuff?

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:38.720
That stuff's good...

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.620
I could get addicted!

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.960
I need to go by the bookstore.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.680
Again?

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:47.330
Don't spend all your time reading smut.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.200
See ya!

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.370
Yeah.

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:09.290
I'm home.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.470
Welcome home.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:14.970
<i>Since we're all here, we'll reveal 
our faces, names, hometowns,</i>

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:16.800
<i>horoscopes, blood types, chronic diseases,</i>

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:20.840
<i>favorite Edo shoguns, favorite Muromachi 
advisors, favorite Kamakura regents.</i>

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:26.310
Do you have Breton's <i>The Key to the Fields</i>?

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.980
Yes, I believe I do.

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:29.290
I thought you might...

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.440
Good thing I didn't buy a copy.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.640
I'll go dig it out.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:33.320
Hey, Takao...

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.440
Want any more?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.680
No, I'm good.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:36.820
Didn't you have gym today?

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.700
I just stand around when we play volleyball.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.470
Dear, there's more squid left.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:43.600
Oh, then I'll have some.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.060
<i>"To the dearest,</i>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.900
<i>fairest woman</i>

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:13.810
<i>Who sets my heart ablaze with light,</i>

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.300
<i>To the angel,</i>

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:19.440
<i>the immortal idol,</i>

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.440
<i>Greetings in immortality!</i>

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.240
<i>She permeates my life</i>

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.170
<i>Like air impregnated with salt</i>

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:30.740
<i>And into my unsated soul</i>

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:33.490
<i>Pours the taste</i>

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.810
<i>for the eternal.</i>

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.550
<i>Sachet, ever fresh, that perfumes</i>

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:47.970
<i>The atmosphere of a dear nook,</i>

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:52.850
<i>Forgotten censer smoldering</i>

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.400
<i>Secretly through the night..."</i>

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.600
Takao, go take your bath!

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.020
Takao, take your bath!

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.080
Okay!

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:16.000
Drink your milk before it spoils.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.560
You're the only one who 
drinks milk in this house.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:36.740
Morning.

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:38.020
Morning, Azusa-chi.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.630
When do you have math?

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:41.610
Third period.

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.550
Did you watch the finale yesterday?

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:44.400
Yep!

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.730
I cried my eyes out!

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:22.070
Okay, I'll return your math quizzes now.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.030
Aoki.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:23.770
Yes.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:24.740
Abe.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:25.630
Yes.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:27.080
Ueno.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:27.610
Yes.

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:29.220
Urabe.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.130
Yes.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.470
Okuda.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:32.380
Yes.

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:33.950
Kasuga.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:34.680
Yes.

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.370
Try harder next time.

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:47.750
Kinoshita.

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:48.820
Yes.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.680
Hey, Kasuga...

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:54.660
What'd you get?

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:55.560
Gouda.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:57.410
Why should I tell you?

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:59.180
Then what's that book you're reading?

00:15:58.770 --> 00:15:59.100
<b>Flowers of Evil 
Baudelaire</b>

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:00.560
Hey, Yamada!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.040
Huh? What's this?

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:03.410
"Evil"?

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:05.360
Th-That's not the right character.

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:06.660
It's the old character...

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:07.840
Give it back, moron!

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.730
You'd never understand the value of that book!

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:12.460
Wait, are you making fun of me?

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:13.770
Then I'm not returning it.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:15.100
Shut up, stupid!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:17.230
Then do you know who Baudelaire is?

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:17.860
Huh?

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.740
You're the only one who knows that crap.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.200
Next, Saeki!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:22.790
Yes.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.570
Saeki got a 98.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.360
That was our top score!

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:31.920
Wow!

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.240
Good job!

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:37.950
You're amazing, Nanako!

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:39.130
It's no big deal.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:40.950
Didn't you get the top score last time?

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:42.900
Wow...

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:44.630
You probably go to cram school.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.410
Nakamura.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:04.800
Hey, you're supposed to respond.

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:06.240
Oh, yes.

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.630
And Nakamura has our lowest score!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:10.960
Another zero!

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.000
What are you trying to do?

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.140
You left every answer blank.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.470
You think you can survive in the real world—

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:23.360
Shut up, shit-face.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.040
Did you just call your teacher...

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.650
a shit-face?!

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:50.980
Come to the faculty office after school.

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:52.230
Next, Numata!

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:55.560
Hurry it up!

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:56.530
She's crazy.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:57.720
Pull it together!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.750
Nakamura-san is trouble.

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:14.700
So yeah, what's up with her?

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:15.580
Huh?

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:17.200
Nakamura...

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.550
She doesn't scare you?

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:20.500
Oh, I guess?

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:23.480
It's impossible to know what she's thinking.

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.960
She probably doesn't have any friends.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:27.590
It's creepy.

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:29.560
But that felt pretty good.

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.580
Shimoyama was shaking.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.120
Well...

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.670
You couldn't pay me to go 
out with a girl like that.

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:39.070
Eh?

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:40.700
What's that about, Yamada?

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:42.430
You think you're better than she is?

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.390
You couldn't pay anyone to 
go out with you, either.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:46.990
What?

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:48.880
Now look here, Kasuga...

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:50.760
You're no better, either!

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:52.530
We're in the same boat!

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.800
Wrong... I read books!

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.540
So what?

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:58.360
Can you understand literature?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.320
You know...

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:02.640
If I had to pick,

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:04.740
I'd go with Saeki-san...

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.220
Huh?

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:12.500
You know...

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.260
I heard she's got a jungle down there.

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:16.450
Stop it, fool!

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:17.800
What the hell?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.030
It isn't nice to talk about girls like that!

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:21.380
Oh?

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:25.450
Don't tell me... 
Kasuga's got a crush on Saeki?

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:27.900
No... It's not like that.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:30.070
Ah, I see! Yes, I understand!

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:31.930
It all makes sense now.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:34.120
Oh! I left my book at school!

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:35.730
I need to go grab it!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:37.640
What? You're running away?

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:39.840
I am not! I really did forget my book!

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:40.740
Bye!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:45.160
Sure... Right on...

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:47.700
<i>Damn.</i>

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:49.390
<i>That Kojima...</i>

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:52.200
<i>He was insulting Saeki-san.</i>

00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:56.250
<i>That guy could never understand 
how wonderful Saeki-san is.</i>

00:19:57.350 --> 00:20:00.350
<i>Hell, I've had a crush on Saeki-san</i>

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.050
<i>for a whole year now.</i>

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:08.260
<i>She's my muse, my femme fatale.</i>

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:32.920
<b>Flowers of Evil 
Baudelaire</b>

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:35.580
<i>But Saeki-san</i>

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:40.580
<i>has no idea that I read books like this.</i>

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:28.800
<b>Saeki</b>

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:36.310
<b>Saeki</b>

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:23.620
Stupid! Stop it!

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:24.640
You're always reading that book, Kasuga-kun.

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:24.640
It's <i>Flowers of Evil</i>.

00:23:24.640 --> 00:23:26.550
Sounds like something a pervert would do.

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:27.800
But I have nowhere to go.

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.840
Kasuga-kun... I saw you.

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:29.360
It's over...

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:32.280
There's something erotic about her.

00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:32.280
I never realized the path of evil

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:33.930
would be so difficult.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:33.930
In return...

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:36.060
You have to agree to a contract with me.

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:41.060
<b>Watch the next episode, shit-face.
Oshimi Shuuzou</b>
